                    insight_renewed:        `The €8.7M mandate is renewed convincingly: quality (≥75), occupancy (≥78%) and a trust index that proves the orchestra extended you authority. You directed where it bought quality and enabled where it earned discretionary effort — Coblence's craft, performed.`,
                    insight_wire:           `Renewed, but on the wire. You cleared both thresholds yet the ensemble's trust is thin — the panel renews and the orchestra wonders. A more disciplined craft would have held the same numbers with more goodwill.`,
                    insight_numberslost:    `You hit the numbers and lost the ensemble. Quality and attendance cleared the line, but trust collapsed — the kind of authority that holds for one review and walks out the door the next season. Numbers without the room aren't leadership of professionals.`,
                    insight_oneshort:       `One threshold short. The authority renews on quality AND attendance together; clearing one while missing the other loses the mandate. Where did the balance break — too much direction, too little, or a gala that traded one number for the other?`,
                    insight_lost:           `The mandate is lost. The rating, the hall and the ensemble didn't recover together inside the season. Either direction was substituted for craft, or no one steered — and the OSL faces restructuring.`,
                    insight_overleading:    `The over-leading penalty stayed active: you substituted control for craft. Even nominal quality gains read as forced to a panel that can see an over-controlled ensemble. Authority over experts is performed, not imposed.`,
                    insight_trustcollapse:  `Trust collapsed below the line where psychological safety sustains creative output. Heavy-handed correction suppresses the very risk-taking that produces artistic distinction — the trust index and the quality rating are linked.`,
                    insight_starwalked:     `The concertmaster walked and the contagion you didn't contain cost you the gala's draw. Formal authority is weak with experts; the autonomy paradox bit.`,
                    insight_balance:        `Genuine balance: quality, attendance and a healthy trust index moving together. You proved that directing skilled professionals and enabling them are the same craft, calibrated — not opposing forces.`,

                    hint_overleading:       `The over-leading penalty is active — you're directing where you should enable. Cut the interventions that only signal control and let the craft do the work.`,
                    hint_trust:             `Trust is collapsing. With career professionals, controlling correction destroys the discretionary effort that produces excellence — protect autonomy where quality doesn't require direction.`,
                    hint_star:              `The concertmaster has disengaged. Authority over experts is extended by respect, not title — and you need a fallback so the gala doesn't live on one name.`,
                    hint_quality:           `The rating is still below the 75 renewal line. Targeted sectionals on the weak sections — not blanket drilling — are the lever that converts to quality.`,
                    hint_attendance:        `Occupancy is below the 78% target. The gala programme and a protected soloist draw are your levers — but not at the cost of the artistic score the same panel judges.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong balance — quality, occupancy and trust all healthy. Now defend it: name where you directed, where you enabled, and how they moved together.`,

